y &= -2x^2 + 4x - 8 \\
&= -2(x^2 - 2x) - 8 \\
&= -2(x^2 - 2x + 1) - 8 + 2 \\
&= -2(x - 1)^2 - 6
\end{align*}

Now we have $y = -2(x - 1)^2 - 6,$ which is in the standard form. Comparing it to the standard form $y = a(x - h)^2 + k,$ we can see that $a = -2,$ $h = 1,$ and $k = -6.$

The equation of the directrix is given by $y = k - \frac{1}{4a}.$ Substituting the values of $a$ and $k,$ we get:
